  "part10_model_result_interpretation": "The high performance of traditional baseline models (TF-IDF + Logistic Regression Micro F1 = 97.79%, TF-IDF + Linear SVM Micro F1 = 97.27%) vs Fine-Tuned BERT (Micro F1 = 91.33%) is attributable to LEGITIMATE STRONG LEXICAL CLASSIFICATION SIGNALS (Category 1). The dataset narratives contain explicit, highly predictive domain n-grams (e.g., 'husband beat', 'demanded dowry', 'following me', 'private photos', 'colleague at work') that TF-IDF representations capture cleanly with zero neural abstraction overhead. The audit confirms this high baseline performance is NOT caused by data leakage or cross-split train-test duplicates."
